Here is a minimal example that reproduces it;
[ConsoleApp2.zip](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/files/7897224/ConsoleApp2.zip)

It has something to do with it being hosted & stopped from within a WPF application that runs on a STAThread.

I tried a super simple 6.0 WPF app and cannot reproduce the issue, I get a TaskCanceledException when clicking the Stop button.
```
public partial class MainWindow : Window
{
    private HubConnection _hubConnection;
    private CancellationTokenSource cts = new CancellationTokenSource();
    private Task _startTask;

    public MainWindow()
    {
        InitializeComponent();
    }

    private void Button_Click_Start(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e)
    {
        _hubConnection = new HubConnectionBuilder()
            .WithUrl("https://localhost:5000/default")
            .WithAutomaticReconnect()
            .Build();

        _startTask = _hubConnection.StartAsync(cts.Token);
    }

    private async void Button_Click_Stop(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e)
    {
        cts.Cancel();
        try
        {
            await _startTask;
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            Console.WriteLine(ex.Message);
        }
    }
}
```

Please provide a simple repro app in the form of a GitHub repo (not a zip).
